    "caveats": [
      "Day -1 quotes of an after-close announcement are often wide, so a single event's E is noisy; read the distribution, not one bar.",
      "The 30-day IV is event-aware: before day 0 it is interpolated between expiries that span the event only, so the crush is the event variance leaving the 30-day horizon plus any change in ordinary volatility (ADR 0004 \u00a73).",
